{"uid":"53c463f6423f3291","name":"test_the_sdk_drives_deployment_promote_and_rollback_end_to_end","fullName":"tests.test_sdk_against_server#test_the_sdk_drives_deployment_promote_and_rollback_end_to_end","historyId":"4f5bfbc1a11258c68b79b1fe59395ba6","time":{"start":1789061338624,"stop":1789061338797,"duration":173},"description":"Promote, promote again, roll back -- the exact sequence\n    ``caliberctl workflow promote``/``rollback`` (Phase 5.3) wraps.\n\n    The first promotion on a fresh alias has nothing to checkpoint (the\n    server's own rollback-checkpoint stack starts empty); a rollback attempt\n    at that point must fail. The *second* promotion is what pushes the first\n    version onto the checkpoint stack, and that is what rollback then pops --\n    so this drives two versions through two promotions specifically to prove\n    the checkpoint stack, not just one call each of promote/rollback in\n    isolation.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Promote, promote again, roll back -- the exact sequence<br />\n<code>caliberctl workflow promote</code>/<code>rollback</code> (Phase 5.3) wraps.</p>\n<pre><code>The first promotion on a fresh alias has nothing to checkpoint (the\nserver's own rollback-checkpoint stack starts empty); a rollback attempt\nat that point must fail. The *second* promotion is what pushes the first\nversion onto the checkpoint stack, and that is what rollback then pops --\nso this drives two versions through two promotions specifically to prove\nthe checkpoint stack, not just one call each of promote/rollback in\nisolation.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1789060397560,"stop":1789060397561,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{